  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 246 AM EDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nHeat, heat, and more heat. Even though the upper ridge will\nweaken/advect westward, the SAL will take a firmer hold of the\nregion and stick around for much of the period. This will create a\nperiod of unseasonable high temperatures, lower than usual\nthunderstorm coverage, and advisory level heat indices. While the\nbreakdown of the ridge pattern may allow for mid/upper level\nmoisture intrusion, it'll still be battling the SAL. Thus, only a\ngradual increase in PoPs is expected through the week.",
